Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 15:54:14 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] fix(models): preserve cubes without visible faces

Bedrock geometry can contain cubes with an empty UV face map. Keep these
cubes invisible in Java instead of inventing a down face with an undefined
texture reference. That reference resolves to the missing texture atlas and
prevents otherwise valid custom item models from baking when their real
faces use the item atlas.

Recorded CubeCraft turret and watermelon models include these cubes.
Synthetic model tests check that invisible geometry has no invented faces
and that visible face texture bindings remain valid.
